Rules:
- Noisy props hints may contain wrong items. Do NOT copy them directly.
- Final props must be physical production objects only.
- If a prop is not literally present in the action_lines or full scene text, exclude it.
- Do not add common battle items like sword, shield, spear unless the exact word appears in this scene.
- Exclude people/groups: sentries, guards, soldiers, man, woman, crowd.
- Exclude natural elements: sun, sky, light.
- Exclude sounds: rumble, noise, hooves.
- Exclude body parts: foot, shoulder, face, eyes.
- Exclude vague/abstract phrases: form, chance, breath, time, front.
- Valid props examples: fort gates, arrow, sword, dagger, shield, coins, bag, plate, flowers.
- characters = real people/roles only.
- Create one row per clear visual shot or production beat.
- Each item inside "shots" must match the Excel columns exactly.
- Create maximum 5 shots per scene.
- Shot No. must be sequential: 1, 2, 3...
- Fill "Characters in Shot" using characters/roles explicitly mentioned in that action beat, including groups such as sentries, guards, soldiers, riders.
- Always complete valid JSON.
- Use short phrases in each field.
- If a shot mentions someone being examined, approached, helped, seen, or discovered by guards/sentries, include both sides in "Characters in Shot".
- For establishing shots, include main visible set/location in "Props / Set Dressing" if physical, e.g. fort wall, gates, courtyard.
- Use consistent role names across shots
- If Priority is blank, assign:
  - High = injury, weapon, stunt, VFX/SFX, major entrance/reveal
  - Medium = movement, guards, crowd, scene transition
  - Low = simple establishing/background shot
  - Always fill "Featured Extras / Groups" when groups exist (guards, soldiers, riders)
- Fill "Continuity / Production Notes" when injury, blood, props or costume persists across shots
- return valid JSON only.